A two-lane warehouse grid: 3 pick aisles and two cross-aisles,
every span a pair of opposed one-way lanes. Pallets from the pick faces to one dock.
10 replications of 5000 after a 1000 warm-up, arrivals every 3 -- above capacity on
purpose, so that the building rather than the arrival stream is what limits the answer.
