Study 1 -- two-lane aisles: what does adding a cart buy?

  carts    delivered       hw   in system        hw   blocked       hw
  2            443.7      2.0     2007.78     24.92    0.0215   0.0013
  4            834.7      5.3     1132.61     31.14    0.0797   0.0040
  6           1109.4      0.9      525.30     33.21    0.1861   0.0015
  8           1111.0      0.0      522.16     33.53    0.3886   0.0013
  10          1111.0      0.0      523.06     33.02    0.5109   0.0011
  12        DEADLOCK       --          --        --        --       --

  Throughput flattens at 6 cart(s).
  From 6 to 10 carts, deliveries go 1109.4 (+/- 0.9) -> 1111.0 (+/- 0.0): a gain of 1.6
  against intervals summing to 0.9, so it is real but negligible.
  Over the same range fleet time blocked goes 18.6% -> 51.1%.

  At 12 cart(s) the grid **deadlocks**, among 6 transporters.
